  "limitations": [
    "The target is the DFO magnitude, log10(days x severity x area_km2), rounded to 0.1. Given those three numbers the formula is exact. The brief model is given two of them and learns the rest; it is not forecasting impact.",
    "The 14 weather columns were added to the DFO table by an enrichment step this repo did not run. Every event is placed at one of 376 points (often a capital), and spot checks against the Open-Meteo archive at those points disagree on both temperature and rainfall. Treat them as synthetic.",
    "Area, duration and severity are only known once a flood is over and mapped. The brief model cannot be used before or during an event.",
    "The no_size variant drops the formula inputs and the window-summed weather. Its weather inputs are still synthetic, so its skill says how the enrichment was generated, not how floods behave.",
    "DFO records large events from news, agencies and satellites. Small and unreported floods are missing, and reporting effort differs by country and decade.",
    "The temporal test scores 2019-2024 start years. Locations repeat across the split because events are snapped to a small set of points.",
    "This model does not feed the DrainSense map. The map score is the logistic model in model/train.py."
  ]
